 "consistency_note": "No. The confirmed train material is two unrelated clips: a sunny summer daytime suburban Odakyu platform (24.8 s) and a night aerial of the Tobu bridge by Skytree (about 39 s with a train in it). They cannot be cut together as one journey. Landmarks split into three looks: night (Tokyo Tower 63 s, Skytree/Sumida ~102 s) which is internally coherent; overcast-day Tokyo Station (35 s, but winter coats in one and leafy trees in the other); Shibuya (29 s, two of three clips are time-lapse, seasons differ: bare trees vs autumn leaves). A night-only landmark sequence of ~165 s is the only coherent block, and it has no POV to go with it.",
 "sourcing_note": "Hard. Web search restricted to pexels.com returns mostly generic 'train window' / 'train arriving' pages with no city, plus Pexels photo and search-listing pages; queries naming Yamanote, Yurikamome, monorail, Toden returned zero Tokyo train videos. Zero Tokyo train-window/front-view POV clips were found at any resolution. Clips Pexels tags or describes as Tokyo were wrong on inspection: 'Shinkansen' 14938845 is Nagoya (052 phone number), 12689437 is Osaka Midosuji line (Nagai station). Landmarks (Shibuya crossing, Tokyo Station, Tokyo Tower, Skytree) are easy to find. Tool limits: fetch_pexels.sh could not resolve any id above ~21,000,000 (7 of 7 tried), so all 2024+ uploads are unmeasured; and three files whose CDN name says hd_1920_1080 are actually 1280x720 by ffprobe (7365111, 12304241, 4200101: 148 s of confirmed Tokyo landmark excluded for resolution). 27 downloads, all 27 viewed on frame sheets (work/audit/tokyo/sheet_1..4.jpg). Steadiness/season judged from 4 stills per clip (denser for 4722537), not from playback. People/brand notes are from thumbnails and are not a clearance check."
